---
code: K0003
title: Unterminated String
description: "Double-quoted string literal reached the end of the line or file without a closing quote"
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
tags: [parse, lexer, string]
deprecated: False
---

A string literal was opened with [`"`]{.expected} but reached the end of the line (`CR`/`LF`) or end of the file without a matching closing [`"`]{.expected}.

In Kura, double-quoted string literals are single-line only and cannot span across raw line breaks.

Example of erroneous code:

```kura
let greeting = "Hello, Kura!
```

Close the string literal with [`"`]{.expected} before the end of the line (using `\n` if you need an embedded newline):

```kura
let greeting = "Hello, Kura!\n"
```

::: tip
If you meant to include a literal double quote inside the string, escape it as `\"` so it does not terminate the string early.
:::
